Neron Rodder was the man who seized the [[Org/Hildebrandt Corporation/index|Hildebrandt Corporation's]] [[Geography/Færrin/Calaria/Hallia/Hildebrandt Tower|tower]] on Bright Souls Eve to take the vault at its top. Nobody in the building knew his name; from the name and the voice he was taken for a man of [[Geography/Færrin/Istria/index|Istria]].

He brought a company of armed people in among the caterers, sealed the tower, cut its telephone lines and most long-distance magic in and out of it, and had the guests herded together and told they would be freed within the hour. He wore a raiment of deep red, near to fire, the mark of a blessing from the [[Heir of the Plague]], and could spread it into burning wings and fly. Those who stood against him he named impenitent and cursed.

He was killed in the tower, and the book he came for was thrown out of it.
